_adilabad.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","attribution":"Kotarambabu, CC BY-SA 4.0 — Wikimedia Commons https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kotasauraus_adilabad.jpg"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Patanjali_Tadepalli.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","attribution":"Kasyap, CC0 — Wikimedia Commons https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patanjali_Tadepalli.png"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Hussain_Sagar_view_from_birla_science_museum_Hyderabad.jpg/960px-Hussain_Sagar_view_from_birla_science_museum_Hyderabad.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","attribution":"Kavali Chandrakanth KCK, CC BY-SA 4.0 — Wikimedia Commons https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hussain_Sagar_view_from_birla_science_museum_Hyderabad.jpg"}],"highlights":"B. M. Birla Science Museum is an Indian science museum located in Hyderabad, India. Constructed by civil engineer P. A. Singaravelu, it comprises a planetarium, museum, science centre, art gallery as well as a dinosaurium. The museum itself was the second phase of the science centre when it opened in 1990. The centre also houses India's first private Space Museum. The museum is a unique facility which is dedicated to history of the space program of India. The space museum was inaugurated in July 2019 and was curated by Pranav Sharma.","nearestTown":"Hyderabad","trail":{"coords":[[17.4029704,78.4727416],[17.4027401,78.4726962],[17.4024579,78.4726316],[17.4022766,78.4726008],[17.4021586,78.4725742],[17.4019952,78.4725508]],"lengthKm":0.11,"gainM":5,"profile":[513,511,511,514,515,516]},"pois":[{"kind":"parking","lat":17.403662,"lng":78.4695286,"distM":140}],"hillFeatures":["temple"],"bestSeason":"Nov–Mar (driest)","landCover":"Built-up","heritage":"Heritage structures in Hyderabad, India"},{"id":"gn-1258260","name":"Red Hil